    "Description": "P1b (Hill-attack -> Blueprints migration, EQS request/poll slice, architect Architect_Question_7_EQS_Slice.md): Condition_IsAreaQueryResolved rebuilt as a visually-authored AiPrimitive BTreeAction. DOCUMENTED DEVIATION: despite the oracle's 'Condition_' name, this graph is authored Intent=Action (Hostings=[BTreeAction]), NOT Intent=Condition -- a Condition-intent blueprint emits a bool wrapper (TickCore(...)==NodeStatus.Success) that would collapse the still-waiting Running poll to false, destroying the timeout window; V_AiPrimitiveIntent (Stage2_Validate.cs) hard-errors BP1100 'Return Running is forbidden' for Condition intent, confirming Running is structurally incompatible with that hosting. Graph: EventEntry -> Compare(GetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId), Literal Int64 -1L, Equal) -> BranchGuard: True (no request cached -- should not occur in correct topology) -> Return(Failure). False -> FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.IsReady(requestId<-CachedEqsRequestId) [IsPure, TrailingContext=View] -> BranchReady: False (not ready) -> FunctionCall WorldOps.SimTime() [IsPure, TrailingContext=View] minus GetVariable(EqsRequestTime) via a native BinaryOp (Subtract) -> Compare(elapsed, Literal Single 5f, GreaterThan) -> BranchTimeout: True (timed out) -> FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.Free(requestId<-CachedEqsRequestId) [IsPure=false/EXEC, TrailingContext=View] -> SetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId<-Literal Int64 -1L) -> SetVariable(CachedTargetGroupHandle<-Literal Int32 -1) -> Return(Failure) (shared with BranchGuard.True and the area-clear Failure tail below); False (still waiting) -> Return(Running). BranchReady.True (ready) -> FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.TargetCount(requestId<-CachedEqsRequestId) [IsPure, TrailingContext=View] -> Compare(count, Literal Int32 0, Equal) -> BranchClear: True (area clear) -> FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.Free(...) [EXEC, View] -> SetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId<--1L) -> SetVariable(CachedTargetGroupHandle<--1) -> SetVariable(EqsRequestTime<-Literal Single 0f) -> Return(Failure) (shared 3-in-degree merge: BranchGuard.True / timeout-tail / area-clear-tail -- Return is a pure exec-In-only terminal sink, proven safe by HillAssault2_AimAndFireSpecific's multi-in-degree Return merges); False (targets found) -> SetVariable(CachedTargetGroupHandle<-FunctionCall AreaQueryBatchOps.TargetGroupHandle(requestId<-CachedEqsRequestId) [IsPure, TrailingContext=View]) -> SetVariable(EqsRequestTime<-Literal Single 0f) -> Return(Success). Per SC-HA011-5, CachedEqsRequestId is intentionally LEFT SET (not reset to -1) on the Success/targets-found path -- Action_DispatchWaveWithTargets consumes it. GetVariable(CachedEqsRequestId) fans its pure Value-Out pin out to 6 consumers (guard compare, IsReady, both Free calls, TargetCount, TargetGroupHandle); Literal(-1L)/Literal(-1 Int32)/Literal(0f Single) each fan out to both the timeout-path and area-clear-path resets that need the identical constant (pure data nodes fan out freely; only exec Out pins remain single-destination, so the timeout and area-clear chains stay two separate exec sub-chains up to their shared Return(Failure) merge). Curated helpers (AreaQueryBatchOps.IsReady/TargetCount/TargetGroupHandle/Free, WorldOps.SimTime, per architect Q#7-D): Free is IsPure=false/EXEC so its side effect (releasing the batch slot) is never dead-code eliminated; the 5s-timeout arithmetic and all Running/Success/Failure routing stay fully visual (native BinaryOp/Compare/Branch). Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Condition_IsAreaQueryResolved, line 237-278).",
